As an Industrial Cleaning Specialist, your primary responsibility is to clean and prepare returned packaging materials for reuse. This includes removing stickers, barcodes, and labels, as well as occasionally disassembling and reassembling products. The job is both physically active and varied, offering you new challenges every day. If you thrive on being hands-on and enjoy an active role, this is the perfect opportunity for you.

Your key tasks include:

- Cleaning formwork and other packaging materials;
- Removing stickers, barcodes, and labels without damaging surfaces;
- Disassembling and reassembling products as needed.

You’ll work in two shifts: early (06:00–15:00) and late (15:00–00:00), ensuring flexibility and variety in your schedule.

- Proficiency in English;
- Physical fitness and ability to perform active work throughout the day;
- Availability for two-shift work without exceptions.

Are you an experienced forklift operator who feels right at home in a logistics environment? Would you like to work for a stable company where you’ll work alongside a small, close-knit team to ensure everything runs smoothly? Then we have a great opportunity for you!

For a client in Weert, we’re looking for an experienced forklift operator who enjoys working a two-shift schedule. You’ll be joining a large logistics company where safety, teamwork, and a pleasant work atmosphere are key priorities.

What will you be doing?

As a forklift operator, you’ll be responsible for moving goods efficiently and safely within the warehouse. You’ll spend most of your workday operating the forklift. Together with four colleagues, you’ll ensure that all pallets and goods are placed in the correct locations and that outgoing orders are ready on time.

Your duties will include:

- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Picking orders and preparing them for shipment;
- Scanning goods;
- Moving pallets and goods within the warehouse;
- Preparing outgoing orders for transport.

You’ll be operating a forklift with double forks, loading from the side. Do you have experience with this? If so, be sure to read on!

You’ve already gained considerable experience operating a forklift and understand how important it is to work safely and accurately. You’re flexible, keep a cool head during busy periods, and are comfortable working two different shifts.

In addition:

- You have recent experience as a forklift operator;
- You hold a valid forklift operator’s certificate;
- You are fluent in Dutch or English;
- You are available full-time;
- You work with precision and always put safety first.

Would you like to contribute to flawless mail delivery and are you looking for a flexible part-time job? Become a mail preparer at our client in Assen! In this role, you will be responsible for ensuring that mail is correctly sorted and prepared for dispatch.

As a mail preparer in Assen, you are responsible for accurately sorting incoming mail. You will check addresses and shipping details and use various mail processing machines to handle the mail efficiently. The job requires precision and good physical condition, as you will be working primarily on your feet. You should also be open to working overtime to assist your colleagues during backlogs or busy periods.

What we ask for:

- No minimum educational requirements;
- Precision and attention to detail;
- Enthusiastic and motivated attitude;
- You speak either Dutch or English;
